speechtext:
The House resumed from Wednesday, May 24, consideration of the motion of Mr. Mulroney that Bill C-3, and Act to establish the Department of Industry, Science and Technology, to repeal the Department of Regional Industrial Expansion Act and to make consequential amendments to other Acts, be read the second time and referred to a legislative committee; and on the amendment of Mr. Langdon:
That the motion be amended by deleting all the words after the word "That" and substituting the following therefor;
"this House declines to give second reading to Bill C-3 because it fails to clearly define federal government responsibility for regional development, and specifically fails to reflect the requirement under s. 36(l)(b) of the Constitution Act, 1982, that Parliament is committed to 'furthering economic development to reduce disparity in opportunities' ".
